045417] [17592186176041 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "464bf015-9f06-5aaf-8fdd-fd419d351b02" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176157 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176157 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176157 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176157 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176157 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176157 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176157 #edb/ref 1045 "The Joint CDF of Two Continuous Random Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176157 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186176766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176157 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176157 #edb/ref 1050 1020.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176157 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "78ca9e7b-ee37-50b5-a0a2-23ce70dad177" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176766 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176766 #edb/ref 1061 34404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176766 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b7b060dd-8145-5ed5-a8c2-a8eb95b625a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176766 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186177010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176771 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176771 #edb/ref 1061 34459 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176771 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "53468626-afd7-5f4a-a657-a28384a0d43b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176771 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176006 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176772 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176772 #edb/ref 1061 34462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176772 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "efc9ab03-5601-5def-b7a6-fbf53ff13b15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176772 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176834 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176834 #edb/ref 1061 36999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176834 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c07e3c6a-add3-551d-844a-69e71cc56e22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176834 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176846 #edb/ref 1061 38160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176846 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5b16e6cf-8aed-5fa4-a7df-c2fe7ed2bc5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176846 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177010 #edb/ref 1064 "The **joint cumulative distribution function** (or joint CDF) of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X \\leq x,Y \\leq y).\n$$\n\nThe joint CDF gives the probability that the pair $(X,Y)$ will lie inside the infinite rectangular region $\\Delta$ that has its top-right corner at $(x,y)$ and whose sides are parallel to the coordinate axes.\n\n![](images/ee/ee82c6b810f02f8b8380bd97c94cbe491095d17dbadc685ffdca1a54cf9828b8.png)\n\nThe joint CDF satisfies the following properties:\n\n- $0\\leq F(x,y)\\leq 1$\n\n- The **marginal CDF** of $X$ is given by $F_X(x)=F(x,\\infty).$\n\n- The **marginal CDF** of $Y$ is given by $F_Y(y)=F(\\infty,y).$\n\n- $F(\\infty, \\infty)=1$\n\n- $F(-\\infty ,y)=F(x,-\\infty)=0$\n\n- If $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then \n$F(x,y)=F_X(x)\\cdot F_Y(y).$\n\nIf $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x, y)$, we have the following relationship between the joint PDF and joint CDF:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\int^y_{-\\infty}\\int^x_{-\\infty} f(u,v)\\; \\textrm{d}u\\textrm{d}v.\n$$\n\nConsequently, if $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables that are nonzero only over the rectangle $[a, b] \\times [c, d]$, then the joint CDF is \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\int^d_{c}\\int^b_{a} f(u,v)\\; \\textrm{d}u\\textrm{d}v.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177010 #edb/ref 1065 5541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177010 #edb/ref 